To place an SVG icon (like a **reading glass** or **search** icon) to the **right side of an input field**, and make it **clickable**, you can use **HTML and CSS** to position the icon, and **JavaScript** to handle the `onClick` event.

Here's a complete example:

---

### ✅ HTML + CSS + JavaScript Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Search Input with Icon</title>
  <style>
    .search-container {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
      width: 300px;
    }

    .search-container input {
      width: 100%;
      padding-right: 35px; /* Make space for the icon */
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .search-icon {
      position: absolute;
      right: 5px;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      cursor: pointer;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="search-container">
    <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
    <svg
      class="search-icon"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      onclick="handleSearch()"
    >
      <path
        d="M15.5 14h-.79l-.28-.27C15.41 12.59 16 11.11 16 9.5 16 5.91 13.09 3 9.5 3S3 5.91 3 9.5 5.91 16 9.5 16c1.61 0 3.09-.59 4.23-1.57l.27.28v.79l5 4.99L20.49 19l-4.99-5zm-6 0C7.01 14 5 11.99 5 9.5S7.01 5 9.5 5 14 7.01 14 9.5 11.99 14 9.5 14z"
        fill="currentColor"
      />
    </svg>
  </div>

  <script>
    function handleSearch() {
      const query = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
      alert("You searched for: " + query);
      // You can call your function here with the query
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🔍 Explanation

- **`.search-container`**: A container that holds the input and the icon.
- **`input`**: The search input field.
- **`svg.search-icon`**: The clickable SVG icon placed absolutely to the right of the input.
- **`onclick="handleSearch()"`**: Calls the `handleSearch` function when the icon is clicked.
- **`handleSearch()`**: Gets the input value and performs an action (e.g., alert, API call, etc.).

---

### 🔄 Optional: Use a Font Awesome Icon (if you prefer)

If you're using **Font Awesome**, you can replace the SVG with an icon like this:

```html
<i class="fas fa-search search-icon" onclick="handleSearch()"></i>
```

And include the Font Awesome CDN in your `<head>`:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css">
```

---

